pnet_datalink: a QNX backend (interface listing).

pnet_datalink picks a backend per OS and has none for QNX, so the crate does
not compile there ("use of unresolved module backend"). zenoh uses it to list
network interfaces. Add a QNX backend whose interfaces() is the shared
getifaddrs() code -- with QNX's AF_LINK/sockaddr_dl from libc for MAC
addresses -- and whose channel() reports raw data-link channels as
unsupported (that would need BPF bindings for QNX's io-sock).

Applied to pnet_datalink 0.35.0 (the version zenoh-c's Cargo.lock pins) by
ports/zenoh-c/recipe.sh.

Upstream-Status: Pending

